<title>BRAZIL: SOCCER-BRAZILIAN RESULTS/STANDINGS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-BRAZILIAN RESULTS/STANDINGS.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of Brazilian</p>
<p>soccer matches played at the weekend.</p>
<p>Sao Paulo championship</p>
<p> America/S.J.Rio Preto   3    Corinthians		  3</p>
<p> Botafogo/Ribeirao Preto 2    Internacional Limeira    0</p>
<p> Guarani		     2    Sao Paulo		    0</p>
<p> Juventus		    2    Aracatuba		    1</p>
<p> Palmeiras		   5    Mogi Mirim		   0</p>
<p> Portuguesa		  2    Uniao Sao Joao	     1</p>
<p> Santos			5    Portuguesa Santista	0</p>
<p> Sao Jose		    1    Rio Branco		   1</p>
<p>Final standings (tabulate under played, won, drawn, lost,</p>
<p>goals for, goals against, points)</p>
<p>Group One</p>
<p> Palmeiras		 23 14  6  3 58 27 48</p>
<p> Santos		    23 13  7  4 45 23 46</p>
<p> Portuguesa		23 12  7  4 46 33 43</p>
<p> Guarani		   23  7  8  8 37 45 29</p>
<p> Sao Jose		  23  4  9 10 29 40 21</p>
<p> Juventus		  23  5  6 12 38 53 21</p>
<p> Botafogo		  23  4  8 11 22 33 20</p>
<p> America		   23  4  5 14 28 62 17</p>
<p>Group two</p>
<p> Corinthians	     23 13  6  4 51 28 45</p>
<p> Sao Paulo		 23 10 10  3 50 26 40</p>
<p> Uniao Sao Joao	  23  9  6  8 35 32 33</p>
<p> Internacional Limeira 23  7  8  8 35 37 29</p>
<p> Rio Branco		23  7  7  9 30 33 28</p>
<p> Aracatuba		 23  7  5 11 28 32 26</p>
<p> Portuguesa Santista   23  7  5 11 30 45 26</p>
<p> Mogi Mirim		23  6  7 10 28 41 25</p>
<p>Note: The teams play once against the other teams in their</p>
<p>own group, then twice against the teams in the other group. At</p>
<p>the end of this, the top two teams in each group qualify for the</p>
<p>play-offs.</p>
<p>Palmeiras, Santos, Corinthians and Sao Paulo qualify.</p>
<p>Rio de Janeiro championship, third stage</p>
<p> Americano		   0    Botafogo		     1</p>
<p> Fluminense		  2    Flamengo		     0</p>
<p> Vasco da Gama	     4    Bangu			  0</p>
<p>Third stage standings</p>
<p> Fluminense		   3  2  1  0  6  3  7</p>
<p> Vasco da Gama		3  1  2  0  7  3  5</p>
<p> Botafogo		     3  1  2  0  4  3  5</p>
<p> Americano		    2  0  1  1  1  2  1</p>
<p> Flamengo		     2  0  1  1  1  3  1</p>
<p> Bangu			  3  0  1  2  3  8  1</p>
<p>Note: the winners of the first, second and third stages</p>
<p>qualify for the final round. Only the top eight in the first</p>
<p>stage go into the second stage and the top six teams in the</p>
<p>second stage carry on into the third stage. If the same team</p>
<p>wins all three stages, they become champions automatically.</p>
<p>First stage winners - Botafogo  </p>
<p>Second stage winners - Botafogo</p>
<p>Eliminated in the first stage - Itaperuna, America, Olaria,</p>
<p>Barreira.</p>
<p>Eliminated in the second stage - Madureira, Volta Redonda</p>
